course: dictionary
lesson: 5721
title: Loop: a shape that goes round
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A loop is a shape made by a line, string or path that bends round and joins itself, like a circle. To loop means to make a loop or move in a loop. In «repeat 4 times: move 10, turn 90», the same instructions go round again and again, and the shape they draw is a square.
explain: In computing, a loop is a set of instructions that repeats. A «forever» loop never stops. In «n = 0. while n < 20: n = n + 7», the loop goes 0, 7, 14, 21. At 21 the test «n < 20» is false, so the loop stops. Always ask: does the loop have a rule for when it stops?
explain: Loop also has meanings outside lessons. «Keep someone in the loop» means make sure they know what is going on, and «out of the loop» means they do not. The same word can mean a shape, a set of repeating steps or knowing the news, so use the words around it to decide which one.
fact: A loop is a shape made by a line, string or path that bends round and crosses or joins itself.
fact: In computing, a loop is a set of instructions that repeats.
fact: An electric circuit must be a complete loop for the bulb to light: electricity goes from the battery, through the bulb and back again.
fact: «In the loop» means knowing what is going on.
exercise: In computing, what is a loop? | *A set of instructions that repeats | A shape that stops at once | A straight line with no bends | A kind of battery
exercise: «Electricity only flows when it has a complete loop to go round.» What must the loop do for the bulb to light? | Turn into a straight wire | Stop at the bulb | Vanish into the air | *Go from the battery, through the bulb and back again
exercise: Ella says, «She is out of the loop.» What does this mean? | She has tied her shoelaces | She is going round in a circle | She has joined a roller coaster | *She does not know what is going on
test: In «n = 0. while n < 20: n = n + 7», what is n when the loop stops? | 7 | 14 | *21 | 20
test: Loop used as a verb means: | *To make a loop or move in a loop | To sleep | To lose your way | To count backwards
exam: In a loop that doubles each time, 10, 20, 40, 80 comes next. What is the next number? | *160 | 120 | 90 | 100
